# Case of the Uneaten Feast. On turn 1 Bot1 casts it and then five Ornithopters; each entering creature it controls gains it 1
# life ("Whenever a creature you control enters, you gain 1 life"): 25. Before the end step the "Solved" ability is not
# offered (CR 702.169d: activate only if this Case is solved). At the beginning of the end step it has gained 5 life this turn,
# so "To solve" triggers and the Case becomes solved (CR 719.3a). On turn 2 Bot2 bolts two Ornithopters. On turn 3 Bot1
# sacrifices the Case: the creature cards in its graveyard as the ability resolves - the two Ornithopters - may be cast from
# there until end of turn (CR 611.2c), but not the Case itself, which is no creature card (its Plains is untapped to pay {W}).
# Bot1 casts the newer Ornithopter from the graveyard; with it on the stack Bot2 bolts a third, which reaches the graveyard
# after the ability resolved and may not be cast. The Case is gone, so the Ornithopter cast from the graveyard gains no life.
# On turn 5 the older Ornithopter left in the graveyard may no longer be cast either: "until end of turn" is over.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Case of the Uneaten Feast
Ornithopter x5
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Island
Island x10

